<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">8 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 8 November, from 960 to 1932.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/960">960 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,066 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leo Phokas ambushes and destroys a Hamdanid army at Andrassos</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In a mountain pass in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taurus-mountains">Taurus Mountains</a>, Byzantine forces under Leo Phokas the Younger ambushed and annihilated the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sayf-al-dawla">Sayf al-Dawla</a>, Hamdanid emir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a>, whose raids had long troubled the empire.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-byzantine-wars">Arab–Byzantine wars</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamdanid-dynasty">Hamdanid dynasty</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1278">1278 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">748 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Trần Thánh Tông cedes the throne to his son Nhân Tông</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Trần Thánh Tông, second emperor of the Trần dynasty, ceded the throne to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-nhan-tong">Trần Nhân Tông</a> but shared power as retired emperor until his death in 1290. Together they were credited with the victories over the Mongol invasions.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tran-nhan-tong">Trần Nhân Tông</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1291">1291 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">735 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Venice confines its glassmaking industry to Murano</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Venetian law confined most of the city's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glassmaking">glassmaking</a> industry to the islands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murano">Murano</a>, in the lagoon north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. Moving the furnaces removed a fire hazard from the city and kept glassmaking expertise from potential competitors.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/murano">Murano</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1519">1519 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">507 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cortés enters Tenochtitlan and meets Moctezuma</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a> and his Spanish and Tlaxcalan allies were received in the Aztec capital by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moctezuma-ii">Moctezuma II</a>. Within days the Spaniards took the emperor hostage, and the city fell to siege in 1521.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/aztec-empire">Aztec Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hernan-cortes">Hernán Cortés</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moctezuma-ii">Moctezuma II</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tenochtitlan">Tenochtitlan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1602">1602 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">424 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Bodleian Library opens in Oxford</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sir Thomas Bodley's refounded library opened to scholars at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a> with about 2,000 books. It became one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s great research libraries, now holding over 13 million printed items.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1895">1895 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">131 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Wilhelm Röntgen discovers X-rays</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Experimenting with a cathode-ray tube in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a>, Wilhelm Röntgen noticed a glowing screen across the room and identified a new penetrating radiation. X-rays transformed medicine and won him the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Physics.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1923">1923 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">103 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hitler launches the Beer Hall Putsch in Munich</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adolf-hitler">Adolf Hitler</a> burst into a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/munich">Munich</a> beer hall and proclaimed a national revolution. The coup collapsed under police fire the next day; Hitler served nine months of a five-year sentence, writing Mein Kampf.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1932">1932 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">94 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Franklin D. Roosevelt is elected president</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the depths of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-depression">Great Depression</a>, Franklin Roosevelt defeated Herbert Hoover in a landslide. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-deal">New Deal</a> reshaped American government, and he was elected a record four times.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 8 November <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-sigismund-elector-of-brandenburg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-sigismund-elector-of-brandenburg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Sigismund, Elector of Brandenburg</span><span class="tp">1572–1619</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/tomoyuki-yamashita"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/tomoyuki-yamashita.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tomoyuki Yamashita</span><span class="tp">1885–1946</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/prajadhipok"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/prajadhipok.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Prajadhipok</span><span class="tp">1893–1941</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
